---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  BrandIconPlayground,
  BrandIconSizes,
  BrandCatalog,
  InlineCompositions,
  GlyphCompositions,
  TileCompositions,
  ResultCardCompositions,
  StackCompositions,
  BrandNameCompositions,
} from "../../components/BrandIconDemo";
---

<Docs title="Brand Icon">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Brand Icon</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Logos for the apps and models your product connects to. Draw a bare glyph in
    text, a framed tile in lists, or a stack of tiles with names on hover.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><BrandIconPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Brand icon usage"
      code={`import {
  BrandIcon, BrandStack, BrandTile, brandNames,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/brand-icon";

<BrandIcon brand="slack" size="sm" />
<BrandIcon brand="google-calendar" size="inline" />
<BrandStack brands={[{ brand: "gmail", name: brandNames.gmail }]} />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>BrandIcon</code> takes a <code>brand</code> and a <code>size</code>.
      <code>"inline"</code> (16px), <code>"glyph"</code> (20px), and <code
        >"fill"</code
      > draw only the logo. <code>"sm"</code> (24px), <code>"md"</code> (36px, default),
      <code>"lg"</code> (48px), and <code>"xl"</code> (56px) put it in a tile. Near-black
      logos such as GitHub, Notion, and OpenAI follow the text color, so they stay
      visible in dark mode. Logos are decorative; put the app name in nearby text.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
      <BrandIconSizes client:load />
      <BrandCatalog client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Inline and glyph</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>"inline"</code> next to 14px text: buttons, menu options, tool activity,
      and notes. Use <code>"glyph"</code> for 20px slots: file rows, chips, workflow
      steps, and prompt banners.
    </p>
    <InlineCompositions client:load />
    <GlyphCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Tiles</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Brand tile"
      code={`<BrandTile>{icon}</BrandTile>

<BrandTile
  size="action"
  render={<Button variant="ghost" size="icon" />}
  aria-label="Gmail actions"
>
  <BrandIcon brand="gmail" size="fill" />
</BrandTile>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>BrandTile</code> is the frame on its own. Put any icon in it. Its
      <code>size</code> is <code>"sm"</code>, <code>"md"</code>, <code
        >"lg"</code
      >, <code>"xl"</code>, or <code>"action"</code>. An action tile is 36px and
      grows to 44px on touch screens. Use <code>render</code> to make the tile a button,
      link, or popover trigger, then fill it with <code>size="fill"</code>.
    </p>
    <TileCompositions client:load />
    <div class="mt-4"><ResultCardCompositions client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Brand stack</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Brand stack"
      code={`<BrandStack
  brands={[
    { brand: "slack", name: "Slack" },
    { brand: "jira", name: "Atlassian" },
  ]}
  label="Apps this agent uses"
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>BrandStack</code> overlaps small tiles. Each tile shows its name on hover.
      The stack is one image; its name is <code>label</code>, or the item names
      joined with commas. An empty list renders nothing. Set <code
        >--sprout-brand-ring</code
      > to the color behind the stack.
    </p>
    <StackCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Brand names</h2>
    <p>
      <code>brandNames</code> maps every brand to its display name. Use it for labels
      so names match the logos.
    </p>
    <BrandNameCompositions client:load />
    <p>
      Popovers, cards, badges, and prompt rows above are sample code. The
      package draws the logos, tiles, and stacks. Your application owns data and
      actions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      <code>BrandIcon</code> and <code>BrandTile</code> are hidden from screen readers
      unless you give them a role and label. When a tile is a button, give it an
      <code>aria-label</code>. <code>BrandStack</code> is announced as one image with
      every app name, so its hover tooltips are not needed to understand it. Tooltips
      fade in over 120ms; reduced motion turns this off.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
